:* The Shu'Meyo Salt takes away all hate when used, so if you have a PLD tank using 2hour, he should be last to use one, or not use any.

::* This item may be obtained by completing the quest {q:Bombs Away!|Bombs Away!|Bombs Away!} given by {n:Buffalostalker Dodzbraz} at (F-9) in {z:Uleguerand Range}, and is highly recommended.

]
* Head to (J-9) of {z:Uleguerand Range}, jump into a hole on the ground and enter {z:Bearclaw Pinnacle} near {p:Home Point} #2.

:* Closest warp is {p:Home Point} #2. The {p:Unity} warp 128 is probably the next best option if you don't have it.
:* When your party is ready, click on the Wind Pillar and enter the battlefield "Flames for the Dead". Buffs will wear upon entering, so be sure to buff inside the battlefield.
:* You may spend an extended time to buff you and your party, with melees building TP using {i:Sleeping Potions|Sleeping Potion|4161} with an {i:Opo-opo Necklace|Opo-opo Necklace|13143}, and/or using {p:Meditate}.
:* When everyone is ready, pull the Snoll Tzar and unload everything you have on him, doing the most damage possible in the short amount of time by any means.

[Boss Name
Snoll Tzar
>Abilities
* It will use **Hyperthermal Combustion** 3 times throughout the battle, each one doing more damage than the last, making the snoll stronger in the process. The 3rd **Hyperthermal Combustion** ejects you from the battlefield.
* **Arctic Impact:** AoE ice damage (~275 each).
* **Cold Wave:** Nasty AoE Frost effect (31 HP/tick).
* **Hiemal Storm:** Extreme directional AoE ice damage for 200-1400 points.
* **Berserk:** Grants the Berserk effect. This makes the fight much easier, but is rare.
** The area attacks have a fairly small radius.

>Notes
:* The time limit in this battle is technically 30 minutes, although once you engage the {m:Snoll Tzar} you will have 45 seconds to defeat it before it ejects you from the battlefield.
:** This time can be increased by using {i:Shu'Meyo Salt|Shu'Meyo Salt|5267} on it.
:** Take care not to overlap the use of the salt because it will have no effect, wait for the message "The Snoll Tzar shakes off the salt!" before using the next one.
:* **Hiemal Storm** also does quite a bit of damage so healers need to be on their toes during this fight. Don't hesitate to use {p:Benediction} if people are about to die!
:* Popular 2 hours to use during this fight are {p:Mighty Strikes}, {p:Hundred Fists}, {p:Meikyo Shisui}, and {p:Astral Flow}.

]
* After you defeat the {m:Snoll Tzar}, return to {p:Bastok} and speak to {p:Cid} in the {z:Metalworks} again to finish this path.

----
* If you have completed the other 2 paths ({M:Louverance's Path|Promathia Mission 5-3/Louverance's Path|Past Sins}, {M:Tenzen's Path|Promathia Mission 5-3/Tenzen's Path|The Pursuit of Paradise}), {p:Cid} will give an additional cutscene and you can move on to the next Chapter: **{M:For Whom the Verse is Sung|Promathia Mission 6-1|For Whom the Verse is Sung}**.

=4 Optional
* After completing the battlefield, you'll be near the top of the mountain: register {p:Home Point} #1 by crossing the frozen pond (H-8).
** Head south and past the drop, you'll come out at (H-9) and go north into (H-8). The entrance to the {p:Home Point} is a tunnel along the north east wall of the frozen pond.
** Must be no weather for the entrance to be accessible at (H-8), otherwise it's frozen. You can use **//fillmode 1** to see where the entrance is located.
* {q:Out of the Depths|Out of the Depths|Out of the Depths} is available in the {z:Metalworks} from {p:Ayame} (K-7) at the cannonry.
** In {z:Oldton Movalpolos}, a {@i:Moblin Hotrok|1729} {i:Moblin Hotrok|Moblin Hotrok|1729} can be obtained for the next quest.
* {q:A Squire's Test|A Squire's Test|A Squire's Test}, {q:The Trader in the Forest|The Trader in the Forest|The Trader in the Forest}, {q:A Squire's Test II|A Squire's Test II|A Squire's Test II}, and {q:The Medicine Woman|The Medicine Woman|The Medicine Woman} (level 20+) are pre-requisites for a Uleguerand Range quest, {q:Over the Hills and Far Away|Over the Hills and Far Away|Over the Hills and Far Away} (level 50+).
** 'Over the Hills and Far Away' can be progressed in tandem with the next section, Flames for the Dead.
** {@i:Ahriman Tears|921} {i:Ahriman Tears|Ahriman Tears|921} x1 can be obtained in Uleguerand Range for a later quest.
** {@i:Snow Lily|1725} {i:Snow Lily|Snow Lily|1725} can also be obtained from {m:Uleguerand Tigers|Uleguerand Tiger} there, if desired for Louverance's Path.

@end
* Once you have finished all three paths, you may talk to {p:Cid} and continue onto the next chapter.

=2 Trust: Shikaree Z
